Program Accomplishments (130):
 Fiscal Year 2025: Characterization of water column habitats to understand potential impacts from deepwater energy and mineral development in the Pacific Ocean;
BOEM marine long-term monitoring program of rocky intertidal habitats and species adjacent to OPS oil and gas operations in the Pacific region, 2023–2028
University-led offshore analysis of seafloor instability and sediments (OASIS) partnership with applications to offshore safety and marine archaeology..  Fiscal Year 2026: The program anticipates funding scientific research that advances understanding of offshore environments and supports environmentally responsible management of offshore energy and marine mineral resources. Examples include studies of beluga whale feeding behavior and fish and invertebrate communities in Cook Inlet, Alaska; socioeconomic effects of the offshore petroleum industry on Gulf Coast communities; maritime heritage resources in the U.S. Pacific Territories; marine ecosystem characterization; protected species research; cultural resource investigations; and offshore renewable energy environmental studies..

